Package: fewclust
Title: Regression for Clustered Binary Outcomes with Few Clusters
Version: 0.4.3
Authors@R:
    person("Luca", "Vedovelli", , "lucavd@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits regression models for binary outcomes measured
    repeatedly within a small number of groups (clusters), with tests and
    intervals that stay calibrated with few groups and short series.  The
    default is the marginalized multilevel model of Heagerty (1999)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.1999.00688.x> with a convergence check and
    Wald statistics referred to a t distribution; generalized estimating
    equations with a first-order autoregressive working correlation and the
    small-sample sandwich correction of Fay and Graubard (2001)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.2001.01198.x> are the fallback.  The
    corrections of Mancl and DeRouen (2001)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.2001.00126.x> and Kauermann and Carroll (2001)
    <doi:10.1198/016214501753382309> are available, and the sign-flip score
    test of Hemerik, Goeman and Finos (2020) <doi:10.1111/rssb.12369> gives
    a p-value for the smallest designs.  The defaults follow a simulation
    study of these methods.  Fits take the data first, accept bare column
    names and have 'broom' methods returning tibbles.
